.PP
Syntax highlighting via tree\-sitter.
Grammars are \f[CR].so\f[R] files loaded on demand with
\f[CR]dlopen\f[R] \[em] the editor binary doesn\[cq]t bundle any
particular language; you pick what you want.
.SH Commands
.PP
.TS
tab(@);
lw(35.0n) lw(35.0n).
T{
Command
T}@T{
Action
T}
_
T{
\f[CR]:ts on\f[R] \f[CR]:ts off\f[R] \f[CR]:ts auto\f[R]
T}@T{
Enable / disable / auto\-detect highlighting per buffer
T}
T{
\f[CR]:tslang <name>\f[R]
T}@T{
Force a language for the current buffer
T}
T{
\f[CR]:tsi <name>\f[R]
T}@T{
Install a tree\-sitter grammar
T}
.TE
.PP
Auto\-detection uses the buffer\[cq]s filetype (file extension or
shebang).
When it fires, the plugin tries to \f[CR]dlopen\f[R] a grammar called
\f[CR]tree_sitter_<name>\f[R] from the configured grammar directory.
.SH Where grammars live
.IP
.EX
\[ti]/.config/hed/ts/<lang>.so
.EE
.PP
This is what \f[CR]tsi\f[R] writes to.
The library is the compiled grammar for \f[CR]tree\-sitter\-<lang>\f[R]
(e.g., \f[CR]tree\-sitter\-c\f[R], \f[CR]tree\-sitter\-python\f[R]).
.SH Installing a grammar
The bundled \f[CR]tsi\f[R] helper clones the upstream
\f[CR]tree\-sitter\-<lang>\f[R] repository, builds the parser as a
shared library, and drops the result into
\f[CR]\[ti]/.config/hed/ts/\f[R].
.PP
From the shell:
.IP
.EX
tsi python
tsi c
tsi rust
.EE
.PP
Or from inside hed:
.IP
.EX
:tsi python
.EE
.PP
After \f[CR]:tsi\f[R], run \f[CR]:tslang python\f[R] (or just open a
Python file with \f[CR]:ts auto\f[R]) to start highlighting.
.PP
\f[CR]tsi\f[R] needs \f[CR]git\f[R], a C compiler (\f[CR]cc\f[R]), and
network access.
The shared library is built with the same C runtime as hed, so the
grammar runs against the statically linked tree\-sitter runtime shipped
in the editor binary.
.SH Highlight queries
Color decisions come from the queries under
\f[CR]queries/<lang>/highlights.scm\f[R] in this repository \[em] the
same files used by neovim\[cq]s tree\-sitter plugin.
If you write your own queries, drop them at
\f[CR]\[ti]/.config/hed/ts/queries/<lang>/\f[R] and they take
precedence.
.SH Notes
.IP \[bu] 2
The vendored tree\-sitter runtime is statically linked into hed \[em] no
\f[CR]libtree\-sitter\f[R] system package needed.
.IP \[bu] 2
A grammar \f[CR].so\f[R] only works against a tree\-sitter runtime
version it was compiled for.
If \f[CR]:ts auto\f[R] reports a load failure after a \f[CR]tsi\f[R],
the grammar\[cq]s tree\-sitter version drifted from the one bundled in
this build \[em] \f[CR]:tsi <lang>\f[R] again to recompile against the
current runtime.
.IP \[bu] 2
Build hed without highlighting at all:
\f[CR]make WITH_TREESITTER=0\f[R].
The editor compiles cleanly without the plugin or the runtime.
